# Purpose
Keep Next.js usage consistent: App Router, layouts, Server vs Client components, and routing conventions.

## Do / Don't

### DO
DO use the App Router: routes live under `app/`, with `page.tsx` for pages and `layout.tsx` for layouts.
DO use Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when needed (hooks, event handlers, browser APIs).
DO use the file-based routing: `app/dashboard/page.tsx`, `app/services/[id]/page.tsx` for dynamic segments.
DO validate route params at runtime (searchParams, params); treat as unknown, narrow safely before use.
DO use `metadata` export or `generateMetadata` for SEO (title, description, viewport).
DO use functional components with hooks in Client Components; avoid class components.

### DON'T
MUST NOT rename/move route files without **BREAKING** label and migration notes (links, bookmarks).
MUST NOT parse route params unsafely; guard NaN/undefined before using Number(param).
MUST NOT mix Pages Router (`pages/`) with App Router (`app/`); use App Router only.
MUST NOT use "use client" at the top level of layout.tsx unless required (prefer Server layout).

## Structure (App Router)
```
app/
  layout.tsx      # Root layout (metadata, viewport)
  page.tsx        # Home
  (group)/        # Route groups
  [dynamic]/      # Dynamic segments
```

## Completion Checklist
[ ] Routes follow App Router conventions (app/, page.tsx, layout.tsx).
[ ] Server Components used by default; Client only when needed.
[ ] Route params validated before use.
[ ] Metadata/viewport set in root layout for SEO and mobile.
